{
  "title": "Beyond A\u2217: Better Planning with Transformers via Search Dynamics Bootstrapping",
  "authors": [
    "Lucas Lehnert",
    "Sainbayar Sukhbaatar",
    "DiJia Su",
    "Qinqing Zheng",
    "Paul Mcvay",
    "Michael Rabbat",
    "Yuandong Tian"
  ],
  "year": 2024,
  "arxivId": "2402.14083",
  "abstract": "Transformers have achieved impressive results in various tasks, but they still struggle with complex decision-making tasks. This work introduces Searchformer, a Transformer model that solves planning tasks more efficiently than traditional A\u2217 search by learning to predict the search dynamics of A\u2217 and then fine-tuning to find optimal plans within fewer search steps.",
  "sections": [
    {
      "title": "The Core Idea",
      "content": "The core idea is to train a Transformer to predict the search dynamics of A\u2217, which involves expressing the planning task and its optimal solution as a sequence of words or tokens. By doing so, the model can learn to generate the entire search process, including the attempted but failed paths, that leads to an optimal plan. <strong>Search dynamics bootstrapping</strong> is used to fine-tune the model and discover more efficient search patterns.",
      "visualization": {
        "type": "flow-diagram",
