    {
      "title": "How It Works",
      "content": "The Transformer model is trained on a dataset of token sequences that capture A\u2217's search dynamics. The model learns to predict the next token in the sequence, given the context of the previous tokens. By including intermediate computation steps, the model can effectively imitate the computation performed by A\u2217. <strong>Search-augmented models</strong> are trained to predict the entire search process, while <strong>solution-only models</strong> are trained to predict only the optimal plan.",
